  "issue_title": "Add a network-wide deregistrations leaderboard to /leaderboards",
  "issue_body": "## Context\n\nThe issue's current body: \"GET /api/v1/chain/deregistrations \u2014 the deregistration-side twin of the registrations route above.\" That backend route is real and fully wired: `src/chain-deregistrations.mjs` builds a `ChainDeregistrationsArtifact` (schema in `schemas/components/05-subnets.schema.json:4205`), and `workers/api.mjs:2160` routes `GET /api/v1/chain/deregistrations` to `handleChainDeregistrations`. Nothing in `apps/ui/src` consumes it \u2014 no query function, no route, no component. Also: the title says \"to /leaderboards\", but **no `/leaderboards` route exists** in this repo. Today \"leaderboards\" is a `LeaderboardsModule` component (`apps/ui/src/components/metagraphed/leaderboards.tsx`) mounted on the homepage (`apps/ui/src/routes/index.tsx:178`), backed by the unrelated `/api/v1/registry/leaderboards` endpoint (five D1-computed registry-health boards: healthiest, fastest-rpc, most-complete, most-enriched, fastest-growing \u2014 see `LeaderboardRow`/`LeaderboardBoardKey` in `apps/ui/src/lib/metagraphed/types.ts:559-587`). Its row shape (`netuid`, `slug`, `name`, plus a per-board metric) does not match the deregistrations artifact's per-subnet fields, so this cannot be a drop-in board card in that existing grid.\n\n## Requirement\n\nAdd a new `/leaderboards` route (file `apps/ui/src/routes/leaderboards.tsx`, following the file-based routing convention in `apps/ui/src/routes/README.md`) that renders a network-wide neuron-deregistration leaderboard sourced live from `GET /api/v1/chain/deregistrations`, ranking subnets by deregistration (eviction) activity over a 7d/30d window.\n\n## Backend\n\n- Endpoint: `GET /api/v1/chain/deregistrations` (query param: `window` \u2014 `7d` default or `30d`, per `CHAIN_DEREGISTRATIONS_WINDOWS` in `src/chain-deregistrations.mjs:21`) \u2014 already live, no backend changes needed.\n- Query function: **none exists.** Searched `apps/ui/src/lib/metagraphed/queries.ts` for any `chain/deregistrations`/`chainDeregistrations` reference \u2014 there is none (the only existing `*Deregistrations*` symbols are `normalizeSubnetDeregistrations`/`subnetDeregistrationsQuery` at lines 3188/3204, which hit the *per-subnet* route `/api/v1/subnets/{netuid}/deregistrations` \u2014 a different, already-consumed endpoint, not this one). This PR must add the typed query function for the network-wide route (following the existing `queryOptions`/`apiFetch`/normalize pattern used throughout that file, e.g. the sibling `subnetRegistrationsQuery`/`subnetDeregistrationsQuery` pair at lines 3169-3213) **and** the corresponding `ChainDeregistrations`-style type in `apps/ui/src/lib/metagraphed/types.ts`, **and** the UI wiring \u2014 all in one PR. A data-layer-only PR is exactly the failure mode this rewrite exists to prevent.\n\n## Deliverable\n\n- File(s) to change:\n  - `apps/ui/src/routes/leaderboards.tsx` \u2014 **new** file, new `/leaderboards` route (registers itself in the auto-generated `routeTree.gen.ts` on build; do not hand-edit that generated file).\n  - `apps/ui/src/lib/metagraphed/queries.ts` \u2014 add `normalizeChainDeregistrations`/`chainDeregistrationsQuery(window)` next to the existing chain-scoped queries, mirroring `subnetDeregistrationsQuery`'s shape but hitting `/api/v1/chain/deregistrations` with no `netuid`.\n  - `apps/ui/src/lib/metagraphed/types.ts` \u2014 add the `ChainDeregistrations` artifact type (schema_version, window, observed_at, subnet_count, network `{distinct_deregistered_hotkeys, deregistrations, deregistrations_per_hotkey}`, intensity_distribution, subnets[] `{netuid, distinct_deregistered_hotkeys, deregistrations, deregistrations_per_hotkey}`), matching `ChainDeregistrationsArtifact` in `schemas/components/05-subnets.schema.json:4205`.\n- Exact anchor: no existing leaderboards-style page renders this artifact shape, so there's no component to extend \u2014 build the new route using the same page skeleton as `apps/ui/src/routes/explorer.tsx` (`AppShell` + `PageHero` + a window toggle identical to `ExplorerDashboard`'s 7d/30d buttons at lines 249-264, `Suspense`/`QueryErrorBoundary`/`Skeleton` for loading, `ApiSourceFooter` for provenance).\n- What to render: a `StatTile` row for the network rollup (Deregistrations total, Distinct deregistered hotkeys, network deregistrations-per-hotkey \u2014 reusing `StatTile` from `@/components/metagraphed/charts/stat-tile` the way `ExplorerDashboard` does at lines 267-301) followed by a ranked table/list of `subnets[]` (netuid \u2192 subnet name/icon via `BrandIcon`, linking to `/subnets/$netuid` the way `BoardCard` in `leaderboards.tsx:104-119` already links leaderboard rows), each row showing `deregistrations`, `distinct_deregistered_hotkeys`, and `deregistrations_per_hotkey`, sorted by `deregistrations` descending (the artifact is pre-sorted server-side per `chain-deregistrations.mjs`'s `subnets.sort(...)`).\n- Coordination note: this is explicitly the \"deregistration-side twin of the registrations route\" per the issue body \u2014 #3465 (network-wide registrations leaderboard) is the sibling PR and will very likely introduce the same new `/leaderboards` route file plus an analogous `chainRegistrationsQuery`. Whichever of #3465/#3466 merges first should create `apps/ui/src/routes/leaderboards.tsx`; the second should extend that same file with a second section/board rather than re-creating the route, to avoid two competing route files colliding on `/leaderboards`. Coordinate on that file, or ping the other issue's assignee before opening either PR.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] Diff touches at least one file under `apps/ui/src/routes/` (the new `leaderboards.tsx`) in addition to `queries.ts`/`types.ts`\n- [ ] The `/leaderboards` route component imports and calls the new `chainDeregistrationsQuery` via `useQuery`/`useSuspenseQuery`\n- [ ] Renders the network rollup (total deregistrations, distinct deregistered hotkeys, deregistrations-per-hotkey) and a per-subnet ranked list/table from `subnets[]`, each row linking to `/subnets/$netuid`\n- [ ] A 7d/30d window toggle is present and re-fetches via the `window` query param\n- [ ] Loading + empty + error states handled, matching the `Suspense`/`Skeleton` + `QueryErrorBoundary` convention already used in `apps/ui/src/routes/explorer.tsx`, with an explicit empty state when `subnet_count` is 0 (cold data)\n\n## Non-goals\n\n- Do not touch the existing `LeaderboardsModule` (`apps/ui/src/components/metagraphed/leaderboards.tsx`) or its `/api/v1/registry/leaderboards` data \u2014 that is a separate, already-shipped registry-health feature, not this artifact.\n- Do not duplicate #3465's registrations board inside this PR; if #3465 lands first and already created `/leaderboards`, this PR should add a second section to that file rather than re-scaffolding the route.\n- Do not build a subnet-scoped (per-`netuid`) deregistrations view here \u2014 that's the already-consumed `subnetDeregistrationsQuery`/`/api/v1/subnets/{netuid}/deregistrations` pair, out of scope.\n\n## Size\n\nSize: S \u2014 keep this PR small (aim for \u226410 files / \u22641000 LOC).\n\nPart of #2542.",
